  "actions": [
    {
      "id": "is.workflow.actions.comment",
      "p": {
        "WFCommentActionText": "Verb list in, one name per line; the clipboard is the payload; the chosen verb runs on it and the result is shown. No list crosses a shortcut boundary: the two-shortcut version passed [payload, verbs] through Run Shortcut and the list arrived TEXT-COERCED, newline-joined, so the menu offered the payload as a choice (device, 2026-08-29). The prompt is set because unset iOS supplies its own \"Which one?\", which says nothing. Run it with nothing and the prologue supplies a default menu and re-enters, which is the idiom 72 shortcuts in this library carry. It reports every run through Log-Repo, stamped with its own build id, because a stale copy and a fresh copy that failed are indistinguishable otherwise and this session lost hours to that. The build id is a content hash of the chain, substituted by BOTH mirrors."
      }
    },
    {
